    G-PREFIX   D an exact prefix of P, both compile          PASS
    G-N        every seed read on both genomes (768, 768)        PASS
    G-AWAKE    no creature asleep in its 120000 ticks (D 0, P 0 slept)   PASS
    G-REPRO    r = 0 reproduces calibrate: somato D 4.450 P 4.102, expression D 7.244 P 6.782   PASS

  THE REGISTERED READING (margin 0.10 Hz; NO SHIFT iff |Delta| + 2 SE < 0.10,
  SHIFT iff |Delta| - 2 SE > 0.10)
  stage 0's P(NO SHIFT fires | true shift 0) at n = 768: somato 1.000, expression 0.947
  (expression under 0.95 at the cap, printed as registered)

    somato       Delta +0.0240 +- 0.0094   |Delta| +/- 2 SE: [0.0052, 0.0427]   -> NO SHIFT
    expression   Delta +0.0147 +- 0.0180   |Delta| +/- 2 SE: [-0.0213, 0.0508]   -> NO SHIFT

    -> A DRAW, NOT A SHIFT. Appending the comparator does not move somato or
       expression; P's calibrate failure is the single-seed estimate meeting a
       re-rolled stream. (b) is answered and the comparator is cleared of it.
       The remaining blocker is calibrate's single-seed verdict itself: its own
       registration, the owner's call. P's targets are NOT edited to chase a draw.

    Nothing ships.

